---
layout: app-shell.njk
permalink: /f1/
title: "Formula 1 | Stefanos Tzortzoglou"
shell: true
bodyClass: "bg-brand-bg text-brand-text antialiased min-h-screen flex flex-col"
navDrawerOnly: true
signOut: true
bodyScripts:
  - src: "/scripts/f1-page.js"
    type: "module"
  - src: "/scripts/contact-widget.js"
    type: "module"
  - src: "/scripts/palette.js"
    type: "module"
---
<section class="app-page">

  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4 mb-2">
    <h1 class="flex items-center gap-3 text-3xl font-bold text-brand-text">
      {% icon "fa-solid-flag-checkered", "h-7 w-7 text-brand-accent" %}
      <span>Formula 1</span>
      <span id="f1Season" class="text-brand-muted font-normal"></span>
    </h1>

    <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
      <label for="roundPick" class="text-sm text-brand-muted">Round</label>
      <select id="roundPick" class="field w-auto py-1.5 text-sm">
        <option>Loading…</option>
      </select>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div id="status" role="status" aria-live="polite" class="mb-6 text-sm"></div>

  {# --- the chosen round ---------------------------------------------------
     Sessions when it has not run, results when it has, and both mid-weekend - which is the
     state the round selector exists to make reachable. #}
  <section aria-labelledby="round-heading" class="mb-10">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-x-4 gap-y-1 mb-1">
      <h2 id="round-heading" class="text-xl font-bold text-brand-text"></h2>
      <p id="roundWhere" class="text-sm text-brand-muted"></p>
    </div>
    <div id="roundBody"></div>
  </section>

  {# --- where in the world -------------------------------------------------
     A globe rather than a place name, because the thing worth seeing about a calendar is how far
     it throws itself around the world between one round and the next. Every round of the season
     is a dot and the chosen one is lit; changing the round turns the globe to it.

     The dots are drawn into a canvas and no screen reader can reach them, so the canvas is hidden
     from one and the round selector at the top of the page is their text alternative - it names
     every round of the season, which is exactly what the dots are.

     The height is explicit because MapLibre measures its container: without one it renders a
     canvas zero pixels tall, which looks like a map that failed rather than a map with no room. #}
  <section aria-labelledby="map-heading" class="mb-10">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-x-4 gap-y-1 mb-3">
      <h2 id="map-heading" class="text-xl font-bold text-brand-text">Where it is raced</h2>
      <p id="circuitName" class="text-sm text-brand-muted"></p>
    </div>
    <div class="card p-3">
      <div id="f1Map" class="h-72 w-full overflow-hidden rounded-lg sm:h-96"></div>
      <p id="mapNote" class="hint mt-3 px-2 pb-1" hidden></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {# --- championships ------------------------------------------------------ #}
  <section aria-labelledby="standings-heading">
    <h2 id="standings-heading" class="text-xl font-bold text-brand-text mb-1">Championships</h2>
    <p id="standingsAfter" class="text-sm text-brand-muted mb-4"></p>
    <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-brand-text mb-2">Drivers</h3>
        <ul id="driverStandings" class="card divide-y divide-brand-border"></ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-brand-text mb-2">Constructors</h3>
        <ul id="teamStandings" class="card divide-y divide-brand-border"></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</section>
